gfx906: stop being classified as CDNA, and reject fp8 KV cache loudly
=====================================================================

File  : vllm/platforms/rocm.py  (in dist-packages)
Before: md5 d7b5a346ae789a2b409630f0042572ac
After : md5 221a70134a8d22f9d411cc0f7871dc10
Applied by: host_tools/patch_rocm_cdna.py (idempotent, anchor-unique,
            py_compile-gated, auto-rollback on syntax error)
Verified : 2026-09-17, real gfx906 hardware (2x Radeon Pro VII)

Why (two independent, silently-wrong fp8 gates on gfx906)
---------------------------------------------------------
1. `_ON_CDNA` used a plain substring match against `_GCN_ARCH`:
       _ON_CDNA = any(arch in _GCN_ARCH for arch in ["gfx9", "gfx1250"])
   `"gfx9" in "gfx906"` is True, so Vega20/GCN5 was classified as CDNA
   even though the file's own comment two lines above says it must never
   inherit CDNA fast paths. Consequence: `supports_fp8()` returned True.
2. Nothing downstream rejects an fp8 KV cache on ROCm:
   - `TritonAttentionBackend.supported_kv_cache_dtypes` includes fp8,
     fp8_e4m3, fp8_e5m2;
   - the SM89 guard in `v1/attention/backends/triton_attn.py` is wrapped in
     `if current_platform.is_cuda():`, so it never runs here;
   - `_is_supported_kv_cache_dtype()` in
     `v1/attention/ops/triton_reshape_and_cache_flash.py` compares a CUDA
     capability number with the ROCm arch string: "gfx906" parses as
     capability (9, 0), which passes `>= (8, 9)`.
   Net effect: `--kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3` was accepted, while Vega20 has no
   FP8 arithmetic at all - a failure deferred into the kernels.

Both defects are shared with the upstream line and with
`David-Lzy/vllm-gfx906` v0.28 (which likewise defines `_ON_GFX906` but only
feeds it to `on_gfx906()`), so this is an upstream trace-level omission, not
a deliberate opt-in.

