Blast radius (audited on the live image before patching)
--------------------------------------------------------
`on_cdna()` had 4 call sites in the whole package, all in rocm.py:
  429  use_rocm_custom_paged_attention()  -> gfx906 now takes the non-CDNA
       branch, which is gated on `_ON_GFX1X` => returns False either way for
       the production model (head_size=256). No behaviour change today; the
       latent trap for head_size 64/128 disappears.
  779  ViT backend auto-select (AITER FA)  -> untouched in practice, the
       wrapper always passes --mm-encoder-attn-backend TRITON_ATTN
  784  ViT backend auto-select (FLASH_ATTN) -> same
  1004 supports_fp8()                     -> now False on gfx906
`supports_fp8()` consumers are triton_moe / torchao / modelopt quant paths
only; none of them is on the production model's path.

Deliberately NOT changed (documented residuals)
-----------------------------------------------
* `triton_attn.py` SM89 guard: still CUDA-only, unreachable on ROCm.
  Covered by the new platform-level rejection instead.
* `_is_supported_kv_cache_dtype()` still compares a CUDA capability against
  a ROCm arch for the **bfloat16** branch (`has_device_capability(80)` is
  likewise true for "gfx906"), even though gfx906 has no native bf16. Not
  touched because `--dtype float16` is mandatory here anyway and the
  production path never selects a bf16 KV cache. Recorded so the next
  maintainer does not rediscover it as "the same bug, half-fixed".
